{"id":"fig","name":"Fig","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:fig"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Fig","text":"First mentioned in Gen. 3:7. The fig-tree is mentioned (Deut. 8:8) as one of the valuable products of Palestine. It was a sign of peace and prosperity (1 Kings 4:25; Micah 4:4; Zech. 3:10). Figs were used medicinally (2 Kings 20:7), and pressed together and formed into “cakes” as articles of diet (1 Sam. 30:12; Jer. 24:2). Our Lord’s cursing the fig-tree near Bethany (Mark 11:13) has occasioned much perplexity from the circumstance, as mentioned by the evangelist, that “the time of figs was not yet.” The explanation of the words, however, lies in the simple fact that the fruit of the fig-tree appears before the leaves, and hence that if the tree produced leaves it ought also to have had fruit. It ought to have had fruit if it had been true to its “pretensions,” in showing its leaves at this particular season. “This tree, so to speak, vaunted itself to be in advance of all the other …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H1690","lemma":"דְּבֵלָה","xlit":"dᵉbêlâh","gloss":"a cake of pressed figs","kjv":"cake  of figs","count":4,"share":0.15},{"strong":"H8384","lemma":"תְּאֵן","xlit":"tᵉʼên","gloss":"the fig","kjv":"fig","count":7,"share":0.27},{"strong":"H519","lemma":"אָמָה","xlit":"ʼâmâh","gloss":"a maidservant or female slave","kjv":"bondmaid, maid","count":4,"share":0.15},{"strong":"H113","lemma":"אָדוֹן","xlit":"ʼâdôwn","gloss":"sovereign","kjv":"lord, master, owner","count":8,"share":0.31},{"strong":"H2543","lemma":"חֲמוֹר","xlit":"chămôwr","gloss":"a male ass","kjv":"ass","count":4,"share":0.15},{"strong":"H4116","lemma":"מָהַר","xlit":"mâhar","gloss":"to be liquid or flow easily","kjv":"be carried headlong, fearful, haste, hasty","count":3,"share":0.12}],"verses":["1Sam.25.18","1Sam.30.12","2Kgs.20.7","Isa.38.21","Gen.3.7","Num.13.23","Deut.8.8","1Sam.25.19","1Sam.25.20","1Sam.25.21","1Sam.25.22","1Sam.25.23","1Sam.25.24","